{"name":"Butternut Tree","hex":"#cf9a5d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"butternut","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A North American walnut tree, Juglans cinerea.","The wood or bark of this walnut tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butternut"},{"term":"tree","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial woody plant taller and larger than a shrub with a wooden trunk and, at some distance from the ground, having leaves and branches.","Any other plant (such as a large shrub or herb) that is reminiscent of the above in form and size."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To chase (an animal or person) up a tree.","To place in a tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Juglans cinerea","blocks":[{"text":"Juglans cinerea, commonly known as butternut or white walnut, is a species of walnut native to the eastern United States and southeast Canada."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Juglans_cinerea_002.JPG/330px-Juglans_cinerea_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juglans_cinerea","wikidata":"Q630288"},{"title":"Butternut (people)","blocks":[{"text":"Butternut was a term applied to inhabitants of the southern parts of Ohio, Illinois and Indiana in the early to mid-nineteenth century. Many of these settlers originated in the Southern United States, particularly Virginia, Kentucky and North Carolina. The term refers to the dye of the butternut tree, by which their clothes were colored. In the years leading up the American Civil War they generally supported pro-south and pro-slavery positions, often electing Doughface politicians. Their settlements hugged much of the border between free and slave states along the Ohio River."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Ohiorivermap.png/330px-Ohiorivermap.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butternut_(people)","wikidata":"Q104902324"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree","wikidata":"Q10884"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Butternut_nut.jpg/500px-Butternut_nut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Butternut_nut.jpg/500px-Butternut_nut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A butternut","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AButternut_nut.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Juglans_cinerea_%28fossil_white_walnut%29_in_glacial_sediments%2C_Michigan.jpg/500px-Juglans_cinerea_%28fossil_white_walnut%29_in_glacial_sediments%2C_Michigan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Juglans_cinerea_%28fossil_white_walnut%29_in_glacial_sediments%2C_Michigan.jpg/1280px-Juglans_cinerea_%28fossil_white_walnut%29_in_glacial_sediments%2C_Michigan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Juglans_cinerea_%28fossil_white_w